<exercise label="ex-negative-binomial-clinical-trial">
  <title> Clinical Trial Enrollment</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      A medical research team is recruiting volunteers for a specialized phase-II clinical 
      trial. Based on preliminary screening criteria, each applicant who arrives at the clinic 
      independently qualifies for the study with probability <m>p = 0.35</m>. The team screens 
      applicants one at a time until five qualified participants have been enrolled. 
      Let <m>Y</m> be the total number of applicants screened.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <task label="ex-nb-trial-d">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Compute the expected value and standard deviation for  <m>Y</m>. Then write, in context, a one sentence interpretation of your results.
      </p>
    </statement>
</task>

  <task label="ex-nb-trial-b">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Calculate the probability that the fifth qualified participant is the 
        tenth applicant screened. 
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>

  <task label="ex-nb-trial-c">
    <statement>
      <p>
        Find the probability that the research team needs to screen no more than 
        <m>7</m> applicants to fill all five spots.
      </p>
    </statement>
  </task>
</exercise>

   </exercises>

  </section>


